# Layer layout (repository → service → delivery)

Readability goal: **open any file once and know its job** — same structural habits as `references/be-suretyship/internal/auth/`, adapted for WiChat (gRPC MS, HTTP gateway, `wi-shared/exception` + `wi-shared/response`). Comment and spacing detail: `wichat-go-style.mdc`.

## Principles

- **Thin delivery** — bind/parse, call service, write response. No business rules.
- **Service owns domain** — validation, orchestration, map repo errors → `exception`.
- **Dumb repository** — I/O only; plain `error`; no `exception` import.
- **Interface at the boundary** — exported `Xxx` interface, unexported `xxx` struct, `NewXxx(...) Xxx`.
- **Value receivers** on impl methods unless the receiver must mutate shared state (match suretyship default).
- **Inject `logger.Logger`** (`wi-shared/infra/logger`) in service, delivery, and repository when I/O errors matter.

## Helper scope (`pkg` vs `wi-shared`)

| Scope                                        | Where                                                                                                        |
| -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **One microservice** (`ms-*`, `api-gateway`) | `backend/<module>/pkg/` — group by role (`auth/`, `validator/`, `utils/`, …); kebab-case leaf dirs; camelCase `package`; see `wichat-go-style.mdc` + `ms-user/pkg/README.md` |
| **Across services**                          | `backend/wi-shared/` — see [wi-shared/README.md](../../backend/wi-shared/README.md); **no** domain use cases |

**ms-user `pkg/`:** flat role folders — [`backend/ms-user/pkg/README.md`](../../backend/ms-user/pkg/README.md). One level deep (`oauth/google.go`, `db/map.go`); no `oauth/google/google.go` nesting. Import paths directly; **no** re-export from `internal/`.

Do not import another service’s `internal/` or `pkg/` from a different `ms-*` module.

### No re-exports

**Never** add a shim file that re-exports another package’s symbols so callers can keep a shorter import path.

Forbidden:

```go
// internal/auth/repository/errors.go — DO NOT
var ErrNotFound = constants.ErrNotFound
```

Import the **canonical** package everywhere (`pkg/constants`, `wi-shared/exception`, `pkg/db`, …). Do not duplicate `var` / `const` / `func` aliases across packages for “backward compatibility” or “stable API” — update call sites instead.

Allowed in the **same** package only: `type Repository = PgRepository` (interface alias), private helpers, constructors.

## Folder layout (per domain)

```text
backend/ms-user/internal/models/     # <domain>_model.go, <domain>_repository_model.go
backend/ms-user/internal/migrations/ # goose SQL (not on startup)

backend/ms-user/internal/auth/
  repository/          # pg_repository.go, redis_*.go, mock/ (Pg only), test/
  service/
  delivery/grpc/

backend/ms-user/internal/user/
  repository/          # pg_repository.go, mock/ (Pg only), test/
  service/
  delivery/grpc/

backend/ms-user/internal/general/   # operational — delivery only (no repository/service)
  delivery/grpc/       # server.go — userv1.GeneralServiceServer (Health RPC, …)

backend/api-gateway/internal/auth/
  delivery/http/       # public REST only
```

**`internal/general`:** cross-cutting ops RPCs (health liveness today). **Delivery only** — no `service/` or `repository/`. Business domains stay under `internal/<domain>/`.

Payload/DTO structs: `internal/models/<domain>_model.go` per service (e.g. `ms-user/internal/models/auth_model.go`). Bun table structs: `<domain>_repository_model.go` in the same package — not under `repository/`.

### No domain `const` / `type` in repository, service, or delivery

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| Domain / policy **constants** (modes, roles, limits, SQL literals, channel names) | `<module>/pkg/constants/` |
| Domain **models** (DTOs, Redis JSON payloads, service inputs) | `<module>/internal/models/` |
| **Sentinel errors** | `pkg/constants` (ms-user) or `wi-shared/exception` — never a local `errors.go` re-export |

**Forbidden** in `internal/<domain>/{repository,service,delivery}/`: `const` blocks and exported domain struct types. **Allowed:** unexported wiring structs (`service`, `pgRepository`, `server`), repository `PgRepository` / store **interfaces** + constructors, `repository/mock` test state, `_test.go` fixtures.

`internal/config` and `internal/server` wiring may keep operational constants (shutdown timeouts) when not domain-facing.

### ms-user: split `auth` vs `user` repositories

One `PgRepository` per **domain + store**, not one god-file for the whole microservice. Same `*bun.DB` may back multiple repos — wire both in `internal/server/server_run.go`.

| Package | `PgRepository` owns |
|---------|---------------------|
| `internal/user/repository/` | Users, identities (Google link), groups, instance settings |
| `internal/auth/repository/` | Sessions, refresh tokens; Redis stores (`EmailAuthStore`, `PasswordResetStore`) in separate files |

Auth **service** today orchestrates both: inject `userrepo.PgRepository` and `authrepo.PgRepository` as separate deps (`s.users`, `s.sessions`). Do not merge back into a single mega-interface unless the domain boundary changes.

See [ms-user/internal/auth/README.md](../../backend/ms-user/internal/auth/README.md) and [ms-user/internal/user/README.md](../../backend/ms-user/internal/user/README.md).

## Repository

Pattern (one backing store per file is fine):

```go
package repository

type PgRepository interface {
    FindUserByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*User, error)
}

type pgRepository struct {
    db  *bun.DB
    log logger.Logger // optional
}

func NewPgRepository(db *bun.DB, log logger.Logger) PgRepository {
    return pgRepository{db: db, log: log}
}

func (r pgRepository) FindUserByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*User, error) {
    // I/O only — no business branching beyond mapping driver errors
}

}
// private helpers for this file only — below all interface methods (see wichat-go-style.mdc)
```

**`pg_repository.go` file order (required):**

1. `PgRepository` interface (+ `NewPgRepository`, struct)
2. Every interface method, **same order as the interface**
3. File-local private helpers only (`findUserBy`, tx helpers, …) — **nothing** off-interface between public methods
4. Driver error mapping → `pkg/db` (`pgErr`) (not private `mapNotFound` in the repo file when shared across repos)

Checklist:

- `context.Context` first on every method.
- Name interfaces by store: `PgRepository`, `RedisRepository` (or `EmailAuthStore`, … for Redis).
- **Postgres hybrid:** Bun (`*bun.DB` over `database/sql` + pgx) for simple CRUD; keep locks, `FOR UPDATE`, joins, and bulk deletes in `sql_queries.go` + `NewRaw` inside `RunInTx`.
- Contract + `pgRepository` live in `pg_repository.go` (no separate `repository.go`).
- Sentinel errors: define in `ms-*/pkg/constants` (or domain-specific `pkg`); repositories and services use `errors.Is(err, constants.ErrNotFound)` — service maps to `exception`.
- No i18n, no HTTP/gRPC, no `wi-shared/exception`.

### Repository mocks and Redis in tests

| Store | In-memory test double | Where |
| ----- | --------------------- | ----- |
| **Postgres** (`PgRepository`) | Yes — `repository/mock/pg_repository_mock.go` + shared `State` when needed | Service tests and any caller that must avoid Docker/testcontainers |
| **Redis** (`EmailAuthStore`, `PasswordResetStore`, …) | **No** `repository/mock/` | Use **[miniredis](https://github.com/alicebob/miniredis)** + the **real** `NewRedis*Store(rdb)` implementation |

- Mock file pairs with production: `pg_repository.go` → `mock/pg_repository_mock.go`; constructor `NewPgRepositoryMock` mirrors `NewPgRepository`.
- Do **not** add Redis “mock” structs that reimplement OTP/TTL/strike logic — that duplicates `redis_*.go`. Do **not** put miniredis wiring in `repository/mock/` (misleading name); use helpers in `repository/test/` or `service/test/`.
- **Do not** put fat fakes in `service/test/` (e.g. `fake_repository.go`) — import `user/repository/mock` and `auth/repository/mock` instead.
- Postgres **integration** tests stay in `repository/test/` (testcontainers when Docker is available).

## Service

Package name **`service`** (not `usecase`). One **domain** per folder under `internal/<domain>/service/` (e.g. `auth`, `user`, `group` in ms-user). Deps are **repository interfaces** (and config/logger), injected via `NewService`.

### Service folder layout (required)

```text
internal/<domain>/service/
  service.go           # only production Go file in this folder
  test/
    service_test.go    # only test file (package <domain>_test or service_test)
```

- **No** sibling `register.go`, `groups.go`, … next to `service.go` — merge into `service.go` or split by **domain package**, not by file in one package.
- **No** `helpers_test.go`, `groups_test.go`, … — one `service_test.go` per domain; shared test wiring → `ms-*/pkg/test-support` (`testSupport`; import only from `*_test`).
- DTOs → `internal/models/`; sentinels and shared limits → `ms-*/pkg/constants`; reusable pure logic → `ms-*/pkg/` (or `wi-shared/` when cross-service).

**ms-user (reference):** `auth/service` (credentials, sessions, OAuth, password reset); `user/service` (instance setup, guest user creation); `group/service` (membership). gRPC `AuthService` delivery may inject all three; proto unchanged.

```go
package service

type Service interface {
    Login(ctx context.Context, in *model.LoginInput) (*model.LoginResult, error)
}

type service struct {
    users    userrepo.PgRepository
    sessions authrepo.PgRepository
    log      logger.Logger
}

func NewService(users userrepo.PgRepository, sessions authrepo.PgRepository, log logger.Logger) Service {
    return service{users: users, sessions: sessions, log: log}
}

func (s service) Login(ctx context.Context, in *model.LoginInput) (*model.LoginResult, error) {
    // Validation
    if in.Email == "" {
        return nil, exception.InvalidInput(exception.MsgInvalidInput, map[string]any{"field": "email"})
    }

    // Repository
    u, err := s.users.FindByEmail(ctx, in.Email)
    if err != nil {
        if errors.Is(err, constants.ErrNotFound) {
            return nil, exception.Unauthenticated(exception.MsgInvalidCredentials, nil)
        }
        return nil, err // raw infra → delivery/grpc → 500
    }

    // Domain logic ...
    return &model.LoginResult{...}, nil
}
```

Checklist:

- Step comments: `// Validation`, `// Repository`, … — same order in every method (`wichat-go-style.mdc`).
- Return `exception.*` with **`MessageCode` consts** only (no hardcoded user-facing sentences).
- Constants / magic values at top of file in `const` blocks.
- Do not import `response/http` or `response/grpc` here.

## Delivery

### HTTP (api-gateway) — `delivery/http`

```go
type Handler interface {
    Login(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
}

type handler struct {
    svc service.Service
    log logger.Logger
}

func NewHandler(svc service.Service, log logger.Logger) Handler {
    return handler{svc: svc, log: log}
}

func (h handler) Login(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    // Bind
    var in model.LoginInput
    if err := json.NewDecoder(r.Body).Decode(&in); err != nil {
        responsehttp.WriteError(w, r, exception.InvalidInput(exception.MsgInvalidInput, nil))
        return
    }

    // Service
    out, err := h.svc.Login(r.Context(), &in)
    if err != nil {
        responsehttp.WriteError(w, r, err, responsehttp.WithLogger(h.log))
        return
    }

    // Response
    responsehttp.WriteJSON(w, http.StatusOK, map[string]any{"data": out})
}
```

### gRPC (microservice) — `delivery/grpc`

```go
func (s *AuthServer) Login(ctx context.Context, req *pb.LoginRequest) (*pb.LoginResponse, error) {
    // Bind (proto → model)
    // Service
    out, err := s.svc.Login(ctx, toLoginInput(req))
    if err != nil {
        return nil, responsegrpc.ToStatus(err)
    }
    // Response
    return toLoginPB(out), nil
}
```

Checklist:

- Same `// Bind` / `// Service` / `// Response` steps.
- Errors: `wi-shared/response` writers only — see [error-handling.md](../../docs/architecture/error-handling.md).
- Cookies/headers in delivery; proto mappers in `ms-*/pkg/*pb`; gRPC `Server` embeds `userv1.*ServiceServer` (wi-shared `models/proto/user/v1` for ms-user).

## Anti-patterns

- Re-export files (`var X = otherpkg.X`) — import `otherpkg` directly.
- One `pg_repository.go` spanning unrelated domains (users + sessions + groups) — split by `internal/<domain>/repository/`.
- Private helpers or off-interface methods **between** exported repo methods.
- SQL/Redis calls in handler.
- `exception` in repository.
- Extra `*.go` files beside `service/service.go` in the same domain — use another `internal/<domain>/service/` instead.
- 200-line **delivery** handlers — split by RPC/handler file; service logic stays in single `service.go` per domain unless the domain itself splits.
- Leaking `err.Error()` from bind/DB to JSON on 5xx.

